title: Redfish Network Adapters
agents: agent_redfish
catalog: hw/server/redfish
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check provides information about the network adaptors of a Redfish compatible device.

 If the device lists the physical ports of an adapter (e.g. HPE iLO), only the
 ports that were up at discovery are monitored. The check goes {CRIT} if such a
 port goes down or is no longer reported, and {WARN} if a port that is not
 monitored comes up. Rediscover the service to monitor the new port.

 A {WARN} or {CRIT} adapter health is reported as {OK} if an unmonitored port has
 the same health. The device does not say what caused the adapter health, so an
 unrelated adapter fault of the same severity is not reported either.

discovery:
 One service is created for each network adapter of the device.

item:
 The id of the network adapter.
